course: dictionary
lesson: 12767
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 2
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The word earthly can mean of this world, of the planet Earth, or at all. Context tells you which one the writer means. Read the words around it first.
explain: «The monk said earthly riches fade, but heavenly treasure lasts.» Here earthly is set against heavenly, so it means of this world, not of heaven. Ask yourself: is the writer talking about heaven, or about this life?
explain: «There was no earthly reason to be late.» Look at the words no and reason. The word earthly makes the no stronger, so it means not any reason at all. Try your meaning in the sentence: «There was not any reason at all to be late» still makes sense.
fact: Earthly means of this world, not of heaven.
fact: In church talk, earthly is often set against heavenly, as in «earthly riches» and «heavenly treasure».
fact: With no, any or why, earthly means at all, as in «no earthly reason» or «why on earth».
fact: Earthly can also mean of the planet Earth, as opposed to space.
fact: Check the context: if a word has more than one meaning, the nearby words show you which one fits.
exercise: «The monk said earthly riches fade, but heavenly treasure lasts.» What does earthly mean here? | Made of earth and mud | Very rich and shiny | *Of this world, not of heaven
exercise: «There was no earthly reason to be late.» What does no earthly reason suggest? | A reason found in the sky | *No reason at all | A small reason to be happy
exercise: «From the space station, the astronauts missed the earthly sounds of rain and birds.» Which meaning of earthly fits here? | Of heaven | Made of stone | *Of the planet Earth | Very loud
test: «She did not have an earthly chance of winning the race.» What does an earthly chance mean? | *Almost no chance at all | A very good chance | A chance from the sky | Two chances side by side
test: «Saints taught that earthly things fade, but heavenly things last.» What is the opposite of earthly in this sentence? | Muddy | *Heavenly | Sudden | Bright
exam: Which sentence uses earthly to mean at all? | «Earthly riches can fade away.» | «The earthly life of the monk was simple.» | *«I have no earthly idea where my shoe went.»
